# Copywriting rules

1. No corporate jargon, tech buzzwords, or AI fluff (e.g., synergy, leverage, robust, ecosystem, seamless, cutting-edge, dynamic).
2. All copy must sound like a straight-talking, trusted local blue-collar tradesman talking directly to a property owner or homeowner.
3. Keep headers and descriptions punchy, practical, and focused on reliability, upfront pricing, and quality workmanship.
